The fix for crbug 580847195 (restricted: "Check WebMediaPlayerMS validity
during frame copy operations"): chromium/src main commit
98bfc32342722aa47adf797becc828664da95e33 (main@{#1743112}), merged to the 159
branch as b982b3c894d8 (8154@{#788}). Its 158 merge (Gerrit 8828835) is
pending, as of 8127@{#1871}.

WebMediaPlayerMSCompositor::ReplaceCurrentFrameWithACopy() copies a shared-image
video frame through the shared main-thread context provider; getting that
provider can synchronously flush GPU channel callbacks, which can garbage-collect
and shut down the WebMediaPlayerMS (and post the compositor for deletion) while
the copy still uses the player's video renderer: a use-after-free in the
renderer, reachable from a page playing a MediaStream (e.g. a canvas
captureStream()) in a media element. The fix passes the player's WeakPtr to
CopyFrame(), checks it after getting the provider, and returns without touching
the compositor when the player went away.

This is the main commit's change without its test (web_media_player_ms_test.cc),
regenerated against 158's file (the same at the .37 tag and at #1871; the main
commit's hunks apply to it at offsets only, with no fuzz). The result is
byte-identical to the file of the pending 158 merge's current patchset. Drop
this once 158 gets the fix (check that the merged change is the same).

